<%- include('partials/header', { title, bodyClass: 'content-page' }) %>
<article class="legal-page page-width">
  <% if (document === 'terms') { %>
    <span class="eyebrow">Last updated September 2, 2026</span><h1>Terms of Sale</h1>
    <h2>Product</h2><p>Mortal Nexus is an independently developed Windows companion application for Mortal Online 2. A purchase grants one personal license to use the application and receive future updates while the service remains available.</p>
    <h2>License use</h2><p>Your license key is personal. You may not resell, publish, share, reverse engineer, or use it to provide unauthorized access to another person. Hardware binding and reasonable anti-sharing controls may be applied.</p>
    <h2>Payments and delivery</h2><p>Payments are processed by Stripe. A license is generated after payment confirmation and delivered to the customer account. Keep your account email current and your credentials secure.</p>
    <h2>Refunds</h2><p>Because a digital key is delivered immediately, refund requests are reviewed individually. Duplicate purchases, failed delivery, and confirmed technical incompatibility should be reported promptly. Fraudulent chargebacks may result in license revocation.</p>
    <h2>Availability and changes</h2><p>Features and data may change as the game changes. We do not guarantee uninterrupted service, exact game data, or continued compatibility with every game update.</p>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>Mortal Nexus is not affiliated with or endorsed by Star Vault. Mortal Online 2 and related marks belong to their respective owners.</p>
  <% } else { %>
    <span class="eyebrow">Last updated September 2, 2026</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2><p>We store the account name, email address, password hash, purchase records, encrypted license data, and technical security information needed to keep the service working. Stripe handles payment card details; Mortal Nexus does not store card numbers.</p>
    <h2>How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to authenticate your account, deliver licenses and downloads, prevent abuse, provide support, and maintain purchase records.</p>
    <h2>Service providers</h2><p>Railway may host the website and database. Stripe processes checkout. KeyAuth creates and validates application licenses. Resend may deliver transactional email when enabled.</p>
    <h2>Retention and security</h2><p>Passwords are one-way hashed, sessions expire, and license values are encrypted before database storage. Purchase records may be retained for accounting and fraud prevention.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may request account correction or deletion by contacting <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>. Some transaction records may need to be retained where required by law or payment rules.</p>
  <% } %>
  <h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
</article>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
